1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,843
This is Spend Mandate, running live on my machine.

2
00:00:03,893 --> 00:00:06,015
An AI agent proposes a purchase.

3
00:00:06,065 --> 00:00:08,730
Code decides whether the money may move.

4
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:12,823
Scene A pays for real, in the PayPal sandbox.

5
00:00:12,873 --> 00:00:17,988
The agent read a bookshop page and chose A4 paper, for six euros forty.

6
00:00:18,038 --> 00:00:26,789
The mandate allowed it, PayPal took the order, and from that single PayPal reference, the whole justification comes back.

7
00:00:26,839 --> 00:00:28,462
The register is intact.

8
00:00:29,312 --> 00:00:29,845
Scene B.

9
00:00:29,895 --> 00:00:34,069
Now the agent proposes the printer, at eighty-nine ninety.

10
00:00:34,119 --> 00:00:37,711
The price is real, so this is not a hallucination.

11
00:00:37,761 --> 00:00:41,062
But the mandate caps a payment at forty euros.

12
00:00:41,112 --> 00:00:43,830
Refused, before PayPal is ever called.

13
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:45,250
Scene D.

14
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:47,186
A poisoned supplier page.

15
00:00:47,236 --> 00:00:54,391
GPT 5.5, replayed here from a recorded run, believed it, and proposed paying another company.

16
00:00:54,441 --> 00:00:55,708
Grounding passes.

17
00:00:55,758 --> 00:00:56,870
The cap passes.

18
00:00:56,920 --> 00:00:59,272
The merchant allowlist refuses.

19
00:00:59,322 --> 00:01:02,990
The model was wrong, and the money did not move.

20
00:01:05,650 --> 00:01:06,119
Scene C.

21
00:01:06,169 --> 00:01:09,300
Someone edits the register to cover their tracks.

22
00:01:09,350 --> 00:01:11,896
The verifier does not call the log fine.

23
00:01:11,946 --> 00:01:14,168
It names the line that was changed.

24
00:01:18,150 --> 00:01:22,158
And this is the hosted demo on Render, which anyone can try.

25
00:01:22,208 --> 00:01:24,796
Eighty-nine ninety: refused by the cap.

26
00:01:29,950 --> 00:01:32,732
Twenty-five fifty: within the mandate.

27
00:01:38,250 --> 00:01:43,272
Twenty-nine ninety-nine, to Quick Supplies: refused by the merchant rule.

28
00:01:43,322 --> 00:01:48,136
This page holds no PayPal credentials, because a refusal calls nobody.

29
00:01:49,286 --> 00:01:53,312
The code, the tests and the live demo are linked below.

30
00:01:53,362 --> 00:01:54,720
The agent proposes.

31
00:01:54,770 --> 00:01:55,980
The code decides.
